From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:09:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: battery voltage row and the Q25's learned health
 facts

Settings > Battery > Battery health gets a Voltage row after
Temperature (ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED EXTRA_VOLTAGE, shown as volts with
two decimals). It is a non-strict fact like temperature, gated by the
new profile key health_voltage_supported (NO hides it): missing or zero
reads "Not reported", values outside 2.5-5.0 V (for example a microvolt
unit mistake) read as not plausible.

Host tests cover the voltage rules and the facts a Zinwa Q25 shows with
its profile and kernel patch 0201 (learned cycle count, aging-factor
full-charge capacity, design capacity in uAh): cycles, capacity health,
temperature and voltage are shown; unlearned values read "Not
reported"; the old MediaTek pair (design Q_MAX/10) is rejected.
